l":"","title":"PART IV: THE FAILED MISSION","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"23.","title":"Wilson's Quandary","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"24.","title":"Rise of a New Turkish Nationalism and the Campaign Against Armenia","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"25.","title":"Turkish Confessions: Ottoman Courts-Martial, Constantinople, 1919-1920","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"26.","title":"American Mandate for Armenia","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"27l","title":"New U.S. Oil Policy in the Middle East and the Turnabout on the Armenian Question","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Epilogue : Turkish Denial of the Armenian Genocide and U.S. Complicity.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Notes","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Glossary","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Selected Bibliography","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Acknowledgements","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"links":[{"url":"http://www.loc.gov/catdir/description/hc043/2003044986.html","title":"Publisher description"}],"covers":[6826203],"lc_classifications":["DS195.5 .B353 2003"],"ocaid":"burningtigrisarm00bala","description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"In this groundbreaking history of the Armenian Genocide, the critically acclaimed author of the memoir Black Dog of Fate brings us a riveting narrative of the massacres of the Armenians in the 1890s and genocide in 1915 at the hands of the Ottoman Turks. Using rarely seen archival documents and remarkable first-person accounts, Peter Balakian presents the chilling history of how the Young Turk government implemented the first modern genocide behind the cover of World War I. And in the telling, he also resurrects an extraordinary lost chapter of American history. During the United States' ascension in the global arena at the turn of the twentieth century, America's humanitarian movement for Armenia was an important part of the rising nation's first epoch of internationalism. Intellectuals, politicians, diplomats, religious leaders, and ordinary citizens came together to try to save the Armenians. The Burning Tigris reconstructs this landmark American cause that was spearheaded by the passionate commitments and commentaries of a remarkable cast of public figures, including Julia Ward Howe, Clara Barton, Theodore Roosevelt, Woodrow Wilson, Ambassador Henry Morgenthau, Charlotte Perkins Gilman, Alice Stone Blackwell, Stephen Crane, and Ezra Pound, as well as courageous missionaries, diplomats, and relief workers who recorded their eyewitness accounts and often risked their lives in the killing fields of Armenia. The crisis of the \"starving Armenians\" was so embedded in American popular culture that, in an age when a loaf of bread cost a nickel, the American people sent more than $100 million in aid through the American Committee on Armenian Atrocities and its successor, Near East Relief."},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["ia:burningtigrisarm00bala","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-07-29:W9-AJU-226"],"title":"The Burning Tigris","edition_name":"1st ed.","subjects":["American Foreign public opinion","Human rights","Opinion publique américaine","Genocide","Armenian massacres, 1915-1923","Génocide arménien (1915-1916)","Génocide"],"publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Peter Balakian","oclc_numbers":["51653350"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publishers":["HarperCollins"],"ia_box_id":["IA134609"],"full_title":"The burning Tigris the Armenian genocide and America's response","key":"/books/OL24772332M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL220554A","name":"Peter Balakian"}],"publish_places":["New York"],"pagination":"xx, 475 p. :","subtitle":"The Armenian Genocide and America's Response","lccn":["2003044986"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [441]-453) and index."},"number_of_pages":475,"isbn_13":["9780060198404"],"dewey_decimal_class":["956.62015"],"subject_places":["Turkey","Turquie"],"isbn_10":["0060198400"],"publish_date":"2003","works":[{"key":"/works/OL15863664W"}],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:W9-AJU-226"],"identifiers":{"amazon":["B0002TX4SO"],"better_world_books":["BWBM59235881"]},"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-07-15T04:10:25.293675"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-07-31T01:26:06.306982"}}}}}